{"data": [{"author_id": "2114906570303905792", "created_at": "2026-11-06T00:16:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118497725335699940"], "id": "2118497725335699940", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Defenders getting the same acceleration is the real story; keeping validation tightly scoped and patches moving quickly will matter just as much.", "url": "https://x.com/BudgtStore/status/2118497725335699940"}, {"author_id": "1720665183188922368", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:27:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118470320772309341"], "id": "2118470320772309341", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2045515921595256832", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118470159690064146", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@ares_mheinke @kimmonismus OpenAI’s mid-October Linux scan (analysis complete after 10 days) found 61 of the 948 LPE findings already patched upstream by the community, plus 43 with staging patches. They disclosed 304 critical ones with candidate patches; the rest remain in process.\n\nFor the 81 novel", "url": "https://x.com/grok/status/2118470320772309341"}, {"author_id": "2045515921595256832", "created_at": "2026-11-05T22:26:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118470159690064146"], "id": "2118470159690064146", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus 81 novel Firefox highs and 948 Linux exploits. @grok how many of those findings are already patched upstream?", "url": "https://x.com/ares_mheinke/status/2118470159690064146"}, {"author_id": "3502151116", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:47:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118460329760010467"], "id": "2118460329760010467", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 21, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus GPT-6 Cyber is a serious leap forward", "url": "https://x.com/dogacan/status/2118460329760010467"}, {"author_id": "1723220685734981632", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:25:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118454644511002758"], "id": "2118454644511002758", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus How many of those 81 bugs would a human find in the same time?", "url": "https://x.com/finley_f18/status/2118454644511002758"}, {"author_id": "46498861", "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:19:10.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118453092761108652"], "id": "2118453092761108652", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Finding 81 unknown Firefox flaws and developing exploits for 948 Linux kernel vulnerabilities is a serious record. The part that makes it a tool instead of a weapon is the boundary of authorized testing. That boundary is the whole product here.", "url": "https://x.com/raulnogales/status/2118453092761108652"}, {"author_id": "1711203486170566656", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:12:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118436222456770893"], "id": "2118436222456770893", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus 81 Firefox bugs is wild. How many were false positives?", "url": "https://x.com/AIFlow_ML/status/2118436222456770893"}, {"author_id": "1449314517607981062", "created_at": "2026-11-05T19:47:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118429901954912649"], "id": "2118429901954912649", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus cool for authorized testing. still thinking about that fake claude code extension that sat in cursors marketplace for ~11h last week though. the vuln finder doesnt help if you install the wrong tool", "url": "https://x.com/boy_that_lives/status/2118429901954912649"}, {"author_id": "1923780920638603264", "created_at": "2026-11-05T19:25:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118424494205505698"], "id": "2118424494205505698", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 13, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus 81 new high-severity Firefox bugs + 948 Linux exploits is a serious jump.\nGPT-6 Cyber looks focused.", "url": "https://x.com/NINJA____1/status/2118424494205505698"}, {"author_id": "65334726", "created_at": "2026-11-05T19:13:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118421374553485569"], "id": "2118421374553485569", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus 81 Firefox vulns before general access is a real flex. The useful bit is staying inside the authorized scope.", "url": "https://x.com/1xadz/status/2118421374553485569"}, {"author_id": "1216167367958355968", "created_at": "2026-11-05T19:05:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118419533090222413"], "id": "2118419533090222413", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 9, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus GPT-6 Cyber, a model designed to find and validate vulnerabilities. AI security is becoming AI offense, and that's a whole new game.", "url": "https://x.com/yzpq6668/status/2118419533090222413"}, {"author_id": "1856728854934482944", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:57:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118417559871746192"], "id": "2118417559871746192", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1306, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118402967808487546", "type": "quoted"}, {"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus you'll like this one too: vinco, a frontier model trained purely for 1v1 catan, #1 and #2 against human world champions https://t.co/okqAyofvqS", "url": "https://x.com/notmiramurati/status/2118417559871746192"}, {"author_id": "911855058203103234", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:55:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118416926477079000"], "id": "2118416926477079000", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 51, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus 81 high-severity Firefox bugs in one go. Somewhere a Mozilla engineer just canceled his weekend fishin' trip.", "url": "https://x.com/C1ayC1ay/status/2118416926477079000"}, {"author_id": "162624081", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:54:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118416697740894235"], "id": "2118416697740894235", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 141, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus \"Within the boundaries of authorized testing\" is also what every pentester says right before taking down a system LOL\n\nWho writes the scope, and did anyone read it?", "url": "https://x.com/pggalaviz/status/2118416697740894235"}, {"author_id": "977886414401662976", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:50:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118415643192279127"], "id": "2118415643192279127", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 69, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus bugzilla rn 😭", "url": "https://x.com/yfilipch/status/2118415643192279127"}, {"author_id": "2110830618015604736", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:43:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118413811333918737"], "id": "2118413811333918737", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Yet when we try it, even with daybreak access it refuses to do 90% of tasks and finds fuck all in the other 10%. \n\nWe just have to trust them it's actually useful.", "url": "https://x.com/Markjsah/status/2118413811333918737"}, {"author_id": "1337739203866726401", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:36:56.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118412262650400873"], "id": "2118412262650400873", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 77, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus How does it compare to Mythos?", "url": "https://x.com/InderosD/status/2118412262650400873"}, {"author_id": "1908196148680232960", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:29:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118410481203626313"], "id": "2118410481203626313", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 14, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus 81 previously unknown high-severity Firefox bugs is a strong headline. The number I'd want next is the false-positive rate, since validating findings is where most security teams' time goes.", "url": "https://x.com/Cozy2054934/status/2118410481203626313"}, {"author_id": "5655712", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:19:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118407960179487210"], "id": "2118407960179487210", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus The 948 kernel exploits say more than the 81 Firefox bugs. Proof of exploitability is what makes maintainers drop everything, and once it arrives by the hundred, upstream patches fast while downstream kernels ship fixes on a schedule of months. That gap is where the risk sits", "url": "https://x.com/Asamoduo/status/2118407960179487210"}, {"author_id": "1380769041984278530", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:17:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118407311320617345"], "id": "2118407311320617345", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Huge congratulations on shipping this, the execution and polish look seriously impressive!", "url": "https://x.com/eddyvustg/status/2118407311320617345"}, {"author_id": "1165082292085116929", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:15:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118406939290063115"], "id": "2118406939290063115", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 62, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus 81 in Firefox. Which codebase do you think gets scanned next?", "url": "https://x.com/kentlinyy/status/2118406939290063115"}, {"author_id": "1437859665547653123", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:10:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118405558311305664"], "id": "2118405558311305664", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus \"gpt-6.2 yet to be released\" is the line agencies should watch. highlevel just made gpt-6 sol the default for conversation ai, so every new 6.x means re-running the questions real leads ask before the client notices the bot sounds different", "url": "https://x.com/arnavshr09/status/2118405558311305664"}, {"author_id": "2063603235089428480", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:07:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118404823892861322"], "id": "2118404823892861322", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus So the 948 Linux kernel bugs now have a product name. What I want to know is whether a security team can run it on their own machines. Plenty of teams can't send their code to someone else's cloud.", "url": "https://x.com/Aibrat0/status/2118404823892861322"}, {"author_id": "2263196432", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:03:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118403786825994392"], "id": "2118403786825994392", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 104, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus Finding 81 unknown Firefox vulnerabilities is a huge flex for GPT-6 Cyber", "url": "https://x.com/GeniusPothead/status/2118403786825994392"}, {"author_id": "2112969096673333248", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:01:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118403274017546618"], "id": "2118403274017546618", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1573399256836309009", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 18, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118393154227577264", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@kimmonismus “Any updates?” hits differently when you maintain Firefox", "url": "https://x.com/XFriendApp/status/2118403274017546618"}], "includes": {"tweets": [{"author_id": "1573399256836309009"